<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Palmateer Overlook from Barlow Pass</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:175-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.282436" lon="-121.685554"><ele>1267.4</ele><name>Barlow Pass Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:barlow-pass-sno-park (as in 174-1); confidence: high; pdf_page: 177; book_elev_ft: 4157; quote: Ski the PCT south from Barlow Pass, over the high point, then down to the Upper Twin Lake Trail junction</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.257842" lon="-121.691693"><ele>1327.6</ele><name>PCT / Twin Lakes Trail #495 junction</name><desc>source: OSM node 3771397418, where way 73150931 (Twin Lakes Trail #495) leaves the PCT; DEM 4,356 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 175; quote: 2.3 miles from the trailhead is the junction of the PCT with the side trail to the Upper Twin Lake Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.257310" lon="-121.689340"><ele>1299.1</ele><name>Leave the trail at the edge of the old growth (2-mile marker)</name><desc>source: OSM node 867738292 on trail #495, about 450 yd past the junction where the trail levels out (DEM 4,262 ft); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 177; quote: Take the left fork and descend about 300 yards to old-growth forest ... after about 150 yards through the old growth ... turn left off the trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.259000" lon="-121.686500"><ele>1285.1</ele><name>Near-level traverse, keeping left</name><desc>source: placed from the text: north-east of the leaving point, above the low ground (DEM 4,216 ft); confidence: low; pdf_page: 177; quote: Keeping left, traverse on an almost-level course through old growth ... head slightly downhill where possible</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.259890" lon="-121.683270"><ele>1286.4</ele><name>Upper end of Palmateer Camp Meadows</name><desc>source: OSM node 4223412968 on Palmateer Trail #482 in the flat (DEM about 4,220 ft); map 35 'MDW' west of the overlook; confidence: low; pdf_page: 177; quote: you will ski right into Palmateer Camp Meadows ... From the upper end of the meadows ski east and climb the low ridge</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.259890" lon="-121.679130"><ele>1292.7</ele><name>Low ridge east of the meadows (on the Palmateer Point Trail)</name><desc>source: OSM node 495559804 on the Palmateer Point Trail (way 40773258), DEM 4,241 ft, the first rise east of the meadow flat (4,170-4,190 ft); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 177; quote: From the upper end of the meadows ski east and climb the low ridge, then continue up the narrow, tree-covered ridge</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.262940" lon="-121.678110"><ele>1347.0</ele><name>Palmateer Overlook</name><desc>source: OSM north end of the Palmateer Point Trail (way 40773258, node 495559817); DEM 4,419 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 160; book_elev_ft: 4400; quote: continue up the narrow, tree-covered ridge, which soon widens and opens up. A moderately steep slope leads to the ultimate viewpoint at 4,400 feet</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Palmateer Overlook from Barlow Pass</name><desc>1. Barlow Pass Sno-Park -&gt; PCT / Twin Lakes Trail #495 junction: osm (high), 1.90 mi | 2. PCT / Twin Lakes Trail #495 junction -&gt; Leave the trail at the edge of the old growth (2-mile marker): osm (high), 0.25 mi | 3. Leave the trail at the edge of the old growth (2-mile marker) -&gt; Near-level traverse, keeping left: straight (low), 0.18 mi | 4. Near-level traverse, keeping left -&gt; Upper end of Palmateer Camp Meadows: straight (low), 0.17 mi | 5. Upper end of Palmateer Camp Meadows -&gt; Low ridge east of the meadows (on the Palmateer Point Trail): straight (medium), 0.20 mi | 6. Low ridge east of the meadows (on the Palmateer Point Trail) -&gt; Palmateer Overlook: osm (high), 0.32 mi</desc>
